<div class="k-grid k-grid--2 splash-cards not-content">
  <div class="k-card">
    <div class="k-card__header">
      <h3 class="k-card__title">Only what you use</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="k-card__body">
      <p>
        If you already compile Tailwind, import the kit from source. Unused component CSS stays
        out of the file, so you only ship the pieces you actually put on the page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="k-card">
    <div class="k-card__header">
      <h3 class="k-card__title">Framework Agnostic</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="k-card__body">
      <p>
        Works in a static HTML file, Astro, React, Vue, or anything else that can render a DOM.
        Classes go on real elements. You do not need a React wrapper or a custom-element runtime.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="k-card">
    <div class="k-card__header">
      <h3 class="k-card__title">Accessible</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="k-card__body">
      <p>
        Screen readers need actual HTML controls, not a styled div. The kit stays on those
        elements and only adds ARIA where CSS cannot. Keyboard users get a visible ring. The words
        on the control are still yours to write.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="k-card">
    <div class="k-card__header">
      <h3 class="k-card__title">Warmth</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="k-card__body">
      <p>
        Buttons, fields, and focus rings use a warm orange that is meant to sit easy on the eyes,
        not a neon accent. Building with this UI kit will give your app staying power with your users. They're not going to look away.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
